# Autopus-ADK worker environment
#
# This repository has no .env loader: unlike the backend (which calls godotenv
# in cmd/server and cmd/worker), the ADK reads the process environment only.
# Copying this file to .env changes nothing by itself. Export these values into
# the environment that launches `auto worker ...` -- your shell profile, the
# launchd plist, or the systemd unit.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A2A worker trust (SPEC-ADK-WORKER-TRUST-DEFAULTS-001)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HMAC secret shared with the backend a2a broker. It verifies the per-task
# SecurityPolicy and the control-plane bundle the broker sends: model, reasoning
# effort, pipeline instructions, iteration budget, skill binding.
#
# If this is unset AND AUTOPUS_A2A_ALLOW_UNSIGNED is unset, the worker does not
# start: WorkerLoop.Start returns an error from EnforceSignedControlPlane
# (pkg/worker/loop_runtime.go, pkg/worker/controlplane/enforce.go) before it
# opens the broker connection, and `auto worker validate` exits non-zero. The
# error names this variable and never prints its value. That refusal is
# deliberate -- an unset secret used to mean "verify nothing", which is
# indistinguishable from a deliberately unsigned link.
#
# The value must match the backend's AUTOPUS_A2A_POLICY_SIGNING_SECRET
# byte-for-byte; changing one side alone splits the two ends of the link.
AUTOPUS_A2A_POLICY_SIGNING_SECRET=

# Explicit opt-out for the above, for dev and self-host runs with no broker to
# trust. Absence of the secret is NOT an opt-out; only this variable is.
#
# When truthy, the worker starts and signature verification takes the fail-open
# path, warning once per process. Truthy values follow Go `strconv.ParseBool`
# exactly (true, 1, t, T, TRUE, True) and are NOT trimmed, so " true " reads as
# false and the worker still refuses to start. Left commented out here because
# the enforced default is the safe one.
# AUTOPUS_A2A_ALLOW_UNSIGNED=

# Resulting combinations:
#   secret set                          -> signatures verified (production)
#   secret unset + opt-out truthy       -> starts unsigned, warns once
#   secret unset + opt-out unset/false  -> startup refused

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider credentials (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed when the provider CLI is not already logged in. Absence is not a
# startup refusal: pkg/worker/setup/provider_auth.go falls back to the CLI's own
# credential directory (~/.codex, ~/.gemini) and `auto worker setup` reports the
# provider as unauthenticated with instructions when neither is present.
#
# OPENAI_API_KEY authenticates the codex and opencode providers.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY authenticates the gemini provider.
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
